==Description==

The [[Image:Silk_CubicCurve_6.svg|32px]] '''Silk CubicCurve_6''' command creates a CubicCurve_6 from a ControlPoly6.

</translate>
[[File:11.-CubicCurve_6.png|300px]]
<translate>

{{Caption|A CubicCurve_6 previewing a cubic curve.}}

==Usage==

# Select a [[Image:Silk_ControlPoly6.svg|16px]] [[Silk_ControlPoly6|ControlPoly6]]
# There are several ways to invoke the command.
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Silk_CubicCurve_6.svg|16px]] CubicCurve_6}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Silk → [[Image:Silk_CubicCurve_6.svg|16px]] CubicCurve_6}} option from the menu.
# A '''CubicCurve_6''' object, is created.

== Properties ==

See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].

A  '''CubicCurve_6''' is derived from a [[[Part_Feature|Part feature]], or more precise a {{Incode|Part::FeaturePython}} object, and inherits all its properties. It also has the following additional properties:

=== Data ===

{{Properties_Title|C1 - Inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|Poly|Link}}: Control polygon.
* {{PropertyData|reverse|Bool}}: Default is {{value|False}}. Reverses the parameter direction.

{{Properties_Title|C3 - Identifiers}}

* {{PropertyData|internalName|String}}: The permanent internal FreeCAD name for this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_type|String}}: Default is {{value|CubicCurve_6}}. The workbench class used to create this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_version|String}}: The class version of this object.


